 $t^2$ from $3$ gives an upper bound on $y$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -3,\\quad y\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697911}] [{:answer/feedback "Multiplication by $-2$ reverses the inequality, so $x$ decreases as $t$ increases." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697912}] [{:answer/feedback "$x=2$ occurs at $t=1$, and every smaller value is attained." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697913}] [{:answer/feedback "The vertex for $x$ is at $t=-1$, outside the allowed domain. For $t>0$, the sharper bound is $x>-3$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -4,\\quad y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697914}] [{:answer/feedback "The minimum of $x$ is $-3$ at $t=2$, and the maximum of $y$ is $3$ at $t=0$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -3,\\quad y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697916}] [{:answer/feedback "The value $y=4$ occurs at the allowed parameter $t=2$; a strict parameter bound does not exclude an interior maximum." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697917}] [{:answer/feedback "$t=0$ is outside the parameter domain; the largest allowed value of $x$ occurs at $t=1$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697920}] [{:answer/feedback "The allowed parameter $t=1$ gives $x=2$, so equality must be included." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697921}] [{:answer/feedback "The nonnegative square in $x=(t-2)^2-3$ gives a lower bound on $x$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -3,\\quad y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697922}] [{:answer/feedback "$2$ is the maximum, but larger values of $t$ produce every smaller value of $x$." :answer/type {:db/id #